{"dossier":"D13","entry_points":[{"sids":["kernel/printk/index.c::pi_init","kernel/printk/index.c::pi_setup_module_notifier.alt_1","kernel/printk/index.c::pi_setup_module_notifier.alt_2","kernel/printk/index.c::pi_create_file"],"text":"Early init creates printk dirs, arms notifier and publishes core index."}],"exports":[{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_swap_in_use","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_extents","kernel/power/user.c::is_hibernate_resume_dev","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_state"],"text":"Swap use nonzero when extent root holds nodes. Resume matches device against recorded device."},{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::HIBERNATE_SIG","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_hardware_signature","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_header_flags"],"text":"Hardware signature validates resumed hardware. Header flags go to restoring kernel in header."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/braille.c::_braille_console_setup","kernel/printk/braille.h::braille_set_options.alt_1"],"text":"Braille setup parses brl with comma or equals plus port, errors when port missing. Helper stores options into cmdline."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/printk.c::console_printk"],"text":"Console table holds current, default message, minimum console and default console levels."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/printk.c::log_buf","kernel/printk/printk.c::log_buf_len","kernel/printk/printk.c::log_buf_addr_get","kernel/printk/printk.c::log_buf_len_get","kernel/printk/printk.c::printk_rb_dynamic","kernel/printk/printk.c::prb","kernel/printk/printk.c::__ro_after_init.alt_1"],"text":"Log uses static plus dynamic with readiness flag. Accessors give base and length. Ring selects static."}],"extracts":["4e6e13831ba8e8a8ff22c4ec0f2415e091d7d38f04d9e776a23b8fcb2edede88","513364c296f3684f9c599ed3565ae9579ee9f9e88f875de6a2d72eef6b480043"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::clean_pages_on_read","kernel/power/swap.c::clean_pages_on_decompress","kernel/power/swap.c::hib_end_io","kernel/power/swap.c::decompress_threadfn"],"text":"Cache flush depends on flags. Missing flush where needed can execute stale data."},{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_header_init"],"text":"Header alloc failure halts boot. Early pressure prevents boot."},{"sids":["kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_open","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_write","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_ioctl","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_release"],"text":"Open must unwind pinning. Write must reject missing buffer. Ioctl needs frozen guards. Release handles frozen versus unfrozen."},{"sids":["kernel/power/wakelock.c::__wakelocks_gc","kernel/power/wakelock.c::wakelocks_lock"],"text":"Reclamation must verify inactivity under lock with monotonic age. Free only after removal from tree and list."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::MAP_PAGE_ENTRIES","kernel/power/swap.c::swap_map_page","kernel/power/swap.c::swap_map_handle","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_header.alt_1","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_header.alt_2","kernel/power/swap.c::CMP_HEADER","kernel/power/swap.c::UNC_PAGES","kernel/power/swap.c::UNC_SIZE","kernel/power/swap.c::CMP_PAGES","kernel/power/swap.c::CMP_SIZE","kernel/power/swap.c::CMP_MIN_RD_PAGES","kernel/power/swap.c::CMP_MAX_RD_PAGES"],"text":"Map fits page minus chain. Header fills page packed. Chunk 32 pages plus header with worst rounding. Read 1024 to 8192."},{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::CMP_THREADS","kernel/power/swap.c::hibernate_compression_threads","kernel/power/swap.c::hibernate_compression_threads_setup","kernel/power/swap.c::hibernate_compression_threads_store","kernel/power/swap.c::hibernate_compression_threads_show"],"text":"Thread count defaults to 3 and stays at least 1. Boot and store reject bad or small values."},{"sids":["kernel/power/suspend_test.c::__initdata","kernel/power/suspend_test.c::warn_bad_state","kernel/power/suspend_test.c::setup_test_suspend","kernel/power/suspend_test.c::test_suspend","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_open","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_state","kernel/power/user.c::need_wait","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_read","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_write"],"text":"Suspend exact match else warns and aborts with early capture and post power test. Open needs hibernation with exclusive acquire, direction limits, handle and mode. IO only on page boundaries."},{"sids":["kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_ioctl","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_compat_ioctl"],"text":"Ioctl checks magic, range and privilege with transition and hotplug locks. Compat forwards size and image."},{"sids":["kernel/power/wakelock.c::WL_GC_COUNT_MAX","kernel/power/wakelock.c::WL_GC_TIME_SEC","kernel/power/wakelock.c::wakelocks_gc_count","kernel/power/wakelock.c::number_of_wakelocks","kernel/power/wakelock.c::decrement_wakelocks_number.alt_1","kernel/power/wakelock.c::decrement_wakelocks_number.alt_2"],"text":"Collection allows 100 entries and 300 seconds idle. Counter resets after sweep. Count adjusts only when enabled."},{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::crc_data","kernel/power/swap.c::crc32_threadfn","kernel/power/swap.c::cmp_data","kernel/power/swap.c::compressed_size","kernel/power/swap.c::compress_threadfn","kernel/power/swap.c::dec_data","kernel/power/swap.c::decompress_threadfn"],"text":"Workers use ready and stop without mutex. Controller sets ready and wakes. Worker clears ready then sets stop and wakes. Stop clears ownership."},{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::hib_end_io","kernel/power/swap.c::clean_pages_on_read","kernel/power/swap.c::hib_bio_batch","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_set_swap_area","kernel/power/user.c::compat_resume_swap_area","kernel/power/swap.c::compressed_size","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_holder","kernel/power/swap.c::root_swap","kernel/power/swap.c::hib_resume_bdev_file"],"text":"Completion releases, latches first error and wakes last. Swap refuses busy, decodes, releases prior and records new. Globals track bytes, root and resume."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/internal.h::nbcon_kthread_wake.alt_1","kernel/printk/internal.h::nbcon_kthread_wake.alt_2","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_kthread_should_wakeup","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_irq_work"],"text":"Wake signals queue or does nothing. Should wake false in emergency or panic else checks record. Irq work wakes."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_cpu_emergency_cnt","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::panic_nbcon_pbufs","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_pcpu_emergency_nesting","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::__initdata","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::panic_nbcon_allow_unsafe_takeover"],"text":"Emergency uses process atomic plus per CPU nesting with boot counter plus panic buffers and takeover flag."}],"locks":[{"sids":["kernel/power/wakelock.c::wakelocks_lock","kernel/power/wakelock.c::__wakelocks_gc","kernel/power/wakelock.c::wakelocks_tree","kernel/power/wakelock.c::wakelock"],"text":"Mutex serializes sweep over tree and counters with full hold. Source lock snapshots idle time and active."},{"sids":["kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_open","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_release","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_read","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_write","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_ioctl"],"text":"Sleep lock stabilizes open and release across freeze. Read and write hold only for transfer. Ioctl adds hotplug."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/nbcon.c::__nbcon_context_update_unsafe","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_can_proceed","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_enter_unsafe","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_exit_unsafe","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_reacquire_nobuf"],"text":"Unsafe update refuses clearing after hostile takeover with CAS retry. Entry and exit clear buffer on failure. Reacquire spins."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/printk.c::__down_trylock_console_sem","kernel/printk/printk.c::__up_console_sem","kernel/printk/printk.c::console_lock_dep_map","kernel/printk/printk.c::console_mutex","kernel/printk/printk.c::syslog_lock","kernel/printk/printk.c::console_locked","kernel/printk/printk.c::console_srcu_read_lock_is_held"],"text":"Legacy semaphore wraps with safety. Registration and syslog use separate mutexes. Srcu query delegates."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F4"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_open","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_release","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_ioctl","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_state","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_set_swap_area"],"text":"Session closed to open to frozen to ready to released. Dispatch freeze, image, swap, suspend and platform."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_kthread_func","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_device_try_acquire","kernel/printk/nbcon.c::nbcon_device_release"],"text":"Printer waits, checks stop and emergency, emits one record when usable. Device acquire uses unsafe. Release flushes."},{"sids":["kernel/printk/printk.c::devkmsg_log_bits","kernel/printk/printk.c::devkmsg_log_masks","kernel/printk/printk.c::DEVKMSG_LOG_MASK_DEFAULT","kernel/printk/printk.c::devkmsg_log","kernel/printk/printk.c::__control_devkmsg","kernel/printk/printk.c::control_devkmsg","kernel/printk/printk.c::devkmsg_log_str","kernel/printk/printk.c::devkmsg_sysctl_set_loglvl"],"text":"Devkmsg enabled, disabled and rate limited. Setup warns and locks. Sysctl rejects when locked and restores prior."}],"structs":[{"sids":["kernel/power/swap.c::swap_map_page","kernel/power/swap.c::swap_map_page_list","kernel/power/swap.c::MAP_PAGE_ENTRIES","kernel/power/swap.c::swap_map_handle","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_header.alt_1","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_header.alt_2","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_extent","kernel/power/swap.c::swsusp_extents"],"text":"Map holds sectors plus chain. Handle tracks iteration and checksum. Header packed holds signatures, checksum, image and flags. Extent range under root."},{"sids":["kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_fops","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_device","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_device_init","kernel/power/user.c::snapshot_open","kernel/power/user.c::snapsho